    "Builds directly on the prior 'dispatch agents on their resolved model tier' phase (commit 9c3738a), reusing its agent({model}) wiring pattern, its 'agent() resolves to null on an unknown model id' null-guard convention, and its Stage-0-bootstrap-is-exempt precedent verbatim.",
    "Consumes rdm-core's existing DispatchStep::Mechanical / `rdm model resolve mechanical` CLI surface (rdm-core/src/model_policy.rs, rdm-cli/src/commands/model.rs) as-is — no rdm-core or rdm-cli changes are in scope for this phase.",
    "Must stay consistent with docs/workflow-schemas.md's 'agent() options spike' findings (model: undefined is inert; an unknown model id resolves to null rather than throwing) that the tightened ack/null-handling logic depends on.",
    "The >>> autopilot-loop:begin/end <<< byte-identical-copy convention and its drift gate in scripts/verify-workflow-autopilot.sh must be preserved — any edit to the block requires lib/autopilot.mjs and autopilot.js to be re-synced in the same commit or the drift gate fails the build.",
    "Independent of, and does not touch, the 'rdm-do --auto' wiring phase (Phase 4 of this roadmap), which routes only through dispatch-phase, not autopilot."
  ],
  "summary": "Autopilot's five mechanical agents (fetch-next, estimate-list, estimate-writeback, advance, park) currently inherit the session's top-tier model because no agent() call passes an explicit `model:`. Fix this by adding one new, deliberately unsized bootstrap dep (`resolveMechanicalModel`, mirroring dispatch-phase's Stage-0 fetch exemption) that runs `./target/debug/rdm model resolve mechanical` once at the very top of `runAutopilot`, before the estimate pre-pass and the drive loop; thread the resolved model id as an extra parameter into the five mechanical dep calls (never into the judgment estimator, plan/implement/review, which stay untouched); and stop the run immediately with a loud, clearly-tagged stop reason (still emitting the always-on batched summary) if the lookup comes back empty, rather than silently falling back to the session model. Alongside the sizing change, tighten the three state-writing mechanical agents (estimate-writeback, advance, park) so a null/empty agent result — the exact failure mode an unresolvable model id produces — is treated as a failure rather than silently counted as success: `advance`'s existing `!ack || ack.ok !== false` bug (null counts as success) becomes a strict `ack && ack.ok === true`, `park`'s previously-ignored return value is now checked (with a bounded retry and a loud log line, but never blocking the final summary), and all three writer prompts are updated to require a read-back confirmation (re-reading the persisted field via `rdm phase/task show`) before asserting `ok: true`, so success is verified rather than self-asserted. dispatch-phase is confirmed (not changed) to already size every agent it dispatches with its own Stage-0 bootstrap correctly exempt. All changes land in the copied `autopilot-loop` block shared byte-identically between `.claude/workflows/lib/autopilot.mjs` and `.claude/workflows/autopilot.js`, plus the non-copied schemas/realDeps/driver section unique to the workflow script, with `scripts/verify-workflow-autopilot.sh` extended to cover the new sizing (including an AC-MODEL-style sweep with a bootstrap whitelist and planted-mutation self-test) and the tightened empty-result handling, while updating the harness's shared `makeFakes` so every pre-existing driven-loop test keeps passing with a default resolved mechanical model."
}

